# The callee is declared to return a number and returns 32-bit integers alone: each result comes back as an integer in a register, and the caller combines the two as they are.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="mixed" role=Source
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[first]] = Patchpoint({{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK: Int32 b@[[second]] = Patchpoint({{*}}:CallDirect)
# CHECK-NEXT: Int32 b@[[both]] = BitXor(b@[[first]], b@[[second]], {{*}}:BitXor)
# CHECK-NEXT: Return(b@[[both]], Terminal)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# No double is made or truncated, and no arm stands by for a number that is no integer.
